    "Investigators reported that the suspect is currently located abroad, and the government is pursuing legal action to recover state assets."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Attorney General's Office of Indonesia has officially designated businessman Arif Kurniawan, often referred to as a nickel industry figure, as a suspect in a major money laundering case involving illegal nickel mining operations. Following the investigation by the Junior Attorney General for Special Crimes, authorities executed a search that resulted in the seizure of 55.8 billion Indonesian Rupiah and 37.8 kilograms of gold bars. Prosecutors stated that these actions are part of a broader effort to recover state losses. Reports indicate that the suspect is currently located outside of the country, prompting officials to initiate travel bans and explore legal avenues, including potential in absentia proceedings for major corruption fugitives, to ensure accountability and asset recovery despite the suspect's absence from the jurisdiction. The investigation also extends to at least one involved corporation.",
